  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "frame_get_lazychunk",
    "file": "c-blosc2/blosc/frame.c",
    "description": "In the contiguous in-memory-frame path, the chunk extent check at line 2028 is incorrectly guarded by `if (rc && ...)`. `blosc2_cbuffer_sizes()` returns 0 when a forged chunk header is syntactically valid, so the bounds check is skipped precisely on success. The function consequently returns the attacker-controlled chunk `cbytes` as if that many bytes were available. `frame_decompress_chunk` passes this false size to `blosc2_decompress_ctx`; dictionary parsing then trusts it, accepts an embedded dictionary length, and `ZSTD_createDDict` reads/copies beyond the actual frame allocation.",
    "conditions": "A malformed but outer-header-valid contiguous frame must provide a valid chunk offset and a syntactically valid Blosc chunk header whose declared `cbytes` extends beyond the end of the frame. The chunk must set `BLOSC2_USEDICT` and encode a positive dictionary size within `BLOSC2_MAXDICTSIZE`; the forged chunk `cbytes` must make `initialize_context_decompression` believe that the dictionary is fully present even though fewer bytes remain in the fuzzer input. Decompressing that chunk flows through `blosc2_schunk_from_buffer` -> `blosc2_schunk_decompress_chunk` -> `frame_get_lazychunk` -> `blosc2_decompress_ctx`, after which `ZSTD_createDDict` performs the out-of-bounds read."
  },
